2.7 Storage Permissions

Inspect the current permission implementation before changing it.

Use Android-supported storage APIs.

Where broad media access is necessary and permitted, request the appropriate Android media permissions for the supported OS versions.

For modern Android versions, handle the applicable image, video, and audio permission model correctly.

Account for Android versions where access is limited to user-selected media.

Handle permission denial gracefully.

If permission is denied, explain what functionality is unavailable and provide a clear recovery action.

Do not repeatedly show permission prompts without user interaction.

Do not request MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE unless a legitimate requirement exists and its use is justified.

Prefer MediaStore for indexed device media.

Use Storage Access Framework for manually selected documents and media outside the indexed collection.

